      "math_academy_id": "q-108269",
      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$  Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(10),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X>x)=0.950.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $\\,1.344\\,$ | $\\,1.646\\,$ | $\\,2.180\\,$ | $\\,2.733\\,$ | $\\,3.490\\,$ |\n| $9$ | $\\,1.735\\,$ | $\\,2.088\\,$ | $\\,2.700\\,$ | $\\,3.325\\,$ | $\\,4.168\\,$ |\n| $10$ | $\\,2.156\\,$ | $\\,2.558\\,$ | $\\,3.247\\,$ | $\\,3.940\\,$ | $\\,4.865\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Since $X∼{χ}^{2}(10),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=10.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $10$ | $\\,2.156\\,$ | $\\,2.558\\,$ | $\\,3.247\\,$ | $\\,3.940\\,$ | $\\,4.865\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>3.940)=0.950.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=3.940.$",
